WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:08.320
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the third of August. Can you all hear me? Right, let's get through the stand-up.</v>

00:00:09.699 --> 00:00:14.250
<v Jamie Brennan>Just about. I'm still grieving over the broken coffee machine in the canteen.</v>

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:22.460
<v Grace Liu>The broken coffee machine in the canteen has definitely improved my water intake. Not my mood, mind.</v>

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:27.440
<v Priya Raman>That explains the atmosphere. Thought it was my headset.</v>

00:00:29.649 --> 00:00:34.200
<v Sarah Okafor>Ha. Coffee complaints duly heard, not going on the job list. Completions first?</v>

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:42.439
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I already swapped the filter on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:48.740
<v David Whitfield>That's the one still showing on the old list, is it?</v>

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.570
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, same one. Not a second filter job.</v>

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:59.750
<v Grace Liu>And we finished the repair on the turbine two last night. That's a completion as well.</v>

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.399
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Both closed, then.</v>

00:01:04.969 --> 00:01:11.969
<v Grace Liu>While I'm on, I noticed the boiler feed pump was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:12.519 --> 00:01:14.620
<v David Whitfield>Settled back down on its own?</v>

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:19.260
<v Grace Liu>Yeah. Just an observation, not raising another job out of it.</v>

00:01:19.769 --> 00:01:22.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Worth mentioning, but nothing new agreed there.</v>

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:28.879
<v Grace Liu>And I can't get to the Main Outfeed Conveyor until production gives us a window. Still blocked.</v>

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.870
<v Priya Raman>No window at all, then? Sorry, you clipped out for a second.</v>

00:01:35.489 --> 00:01:39.340
<v Grace Liu>No, nothing available. It's not work we can take on today.</v>

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:48.299
<v Sarah Okafor>Same position here: can't get to the compressor one until production gives us a window. That stays blocked too.</v>

00:01:48.769 --> 00:01:54.019
<v Jamie Brennan>And the shutdown on the Compressed Air Dryer is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.200
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Ah, cancelled rather than just waiting for access?</v>

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.689
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. Off altogether, not another one sitting behind a production window.</v>

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:08.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, no shutdown work on that, then. Let's get onto what we are agreeing.</v>

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:15.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, can you do a site visit at the water works with the contractor? No rush on that.</v>

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:22.610
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, just the site visit with them, rather than any work while we're there?</v>

00:02:24.979 --> 00:02:30.229
<v Sarah Okafor>That's it, Grace. The site visit at the water works with the contractor. No rush.</v>

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:32.969
<v Grace Liu>Fine, I'll do that.</v>

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:35.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. Um, toolbox talk next.</v>

00:02:37.469 --> 00:02:41.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team? Normal priority.</v>

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:47.270
<v Hannah Price>Yeah. Not being bumped up above everything else, then?</v>

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.900
<v Sarah Okafor>No, normal priority on that one.</v>

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:53.819
<v Hannah Price>Okay, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team.</v>

00:02:55.139 --> 00:03:01.090
<v Jamie Brennan>While you're there, where are we with spare parts for the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot?</v>

00:03:02.139 --> 00:03:06.689
<v Hannah Price>I'll order spare parts for the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot today.</v>

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:10.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Hannah Price against that one, ordering today.</v>

00:03:13.139 --> 00:03:14.340
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:20.469
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, I was trying to unmute and hit the hand thing. Nothing to add. Very professional.</v>

00:03:20.789 --> 00:03:24.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Better than hanging up, which I've done. Right, the handover report.</v>

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:31.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you send the shift handover report round on Friday? Low priority.</v>

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.169
<v Jamie Brennan>On Friday, yeah? Not asking for it round today?</v>

00:03:37.669 --> 00:03:40.120
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, on Friday. It's low priority.</v>

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:45.819
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll send the shift handover report round on Friday.</v>

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:49.210
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Anything on the mechanical side?</v>

00:03:51.009 --> 00:03:56.610
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the booster pump. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:57.729 --> 00:04:01.580
<v Olumide Adeyemi>So investigation, not saying we've got a repair to do yet?</v>

00:04:02.939 --> 00:04:09.590
<v David Whitfield>Exactly. I'll investigate the pressure drop first. Not committing to a repair when we don't know what's behind it.</v>

00:04:12.009 --> 00:04:17.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Davey owns the investigation on the booster pump. It matters but it's not urgent, understood.</v>

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.269
<v Jamie Brennan>And the chiller on three? We haven't covered that.</v>

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:31.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, Jamie, can you run a function test on the chiller on three next Tuesday? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:04:32.319 --> 00:04:34.769
<v Jamie Brennan>Still next Tuesday, even with that priority?</v>

00:04:37.029 --> 00:04:42.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, next Tuesday is the timing. But that's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:49.439
<v Jamie Brennan>Understood. I'll run a function test on the chiller on three next Tuesday, first priority.</v>

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie. That's the production hold-up one, not a routine low-priority test.</v>

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.740
<v Priya Raman>Right, got you. Sorry, I spoke over the end there.</v>

00:05:02.189 --> 00:05:04.639
<v Sarah Okafor>No worries. Quality bit before we finish.</v>

00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:13.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, can you write up the near miss at the palletiser by end of day? Top priority please.</v>

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.800
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, that's ahead of the toolbox talk, then.</v>

00:05:18.529 --> 00:05:23.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. The near miss write-up is top priority please, by end of day.</v>

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:31.949
<v Hannah Price>Understood. I'll write up the near miss at the palletiser by end of day. That comes first for me.</v>

00:05:33.259 --> 00:05:36.060
<v Grace Liu>On the risk assessment— sorry, were you finished?</v>

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:39.350
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, go on, Grace.</v>

00:05:39.699 --> 00:05:43.899
<v Grace Liu>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the trucks this morning.</v>

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:48.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace. Risk assessment for work on the trucks, this morning.</v>

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:52.009
<v Grace Liu>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:05:52.879 --> 00:05:59.180
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Think that's my bit covered. Just making sure the filter was heard as a completion, not another job.</v>

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.009
<v Jamie Brennan>Same with the dryer shutdown. Cancelled, not waiting in the queue.</v>

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:10.540
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, both clear. And the access blockers stay blocked; we're not pretending we've got windows.</v>

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.149
<v David Whitfield>Right, cheers. A surprisingly coffee-free meeting.</v>

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Don't remind us. Thanks, everyone. That's us.</v>
